     "Salt March",
     "Quit India",
     "INA"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Mahatma Gandhi returned from South Africa in 1915 and led the freedom movement on the principles of truth and non-violence (satyagraha). He led the Champaran and Kheda satyagrahas and the Ahmedabad mill strike.\nHe launched the Non-Cooperation Movement in 1920 after the Jallianwala Bagh massacre of 1919 and the Rowlatt Act. It was called off after Chauri Chaura. The Civil Disobedience Movement began in 1930 with the Salt March to Dandi.\nThe Quit India Movement of 1942 called for 'Do or Die'. Subhas Chandra Bose formed the Indian National Army. India became independent on 15 August 1947."
    }
